.TH "TRCC\-DISPLAY" "1" "" "trcc\-linux 9.8.4" "TRCC Manual"
.SH NAME
trcc\-display \- Configure device display (theme / orientation / brightness)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrcc display\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure device display (theme / orientation / brightness).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS apply\-mask
.PP
\fBtrcc display apply\-mask\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR
.PP
Override the active theme's mask with a user\-supplied image.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Image file path (png/jpg/jpeg/bmp/webp)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS background\-mode
.PP
\fBtrcc display background\-mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIMODE\fR
.PP
Pick what fills the LCD behind overlays.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBMODE\fR
\&'theme' / 'color' / 'transparent'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS boot\-anim
.PP
\fBtrcc display boot\-anim\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIFRAMES_DIR\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Upload a multi\-frame compressed boot animation to a SCSI LCD's flash. The animation plays from device flash on every boot until overwritten. Only SCSI panels with 240x240 / 240x320 / 320x240 / 320x320 resolution support boot animations. Frame files are picked up in alphabetical order from *frames_dir*  \-  PNG / JPG / JPEG / BMP / WebP. Each frame uses the same dwell time via \-\-delay (per\-frame delays via the API only).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922 (SCSI only)
.TP
\fBFRAMES_DIR\fR
Directory of image frames (sorted alphabetically; 1\-248 frames)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-delay, \-d \fIDELAY_DS\fR\fR
Dwell time per frame in deciseconds (10 = 1.0 s, max 25 = 2.5 s)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS color
.PP
\fBtrcc display color\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIHEX_COLOR\fR
.PP
Display a single solid color on the LCD. Smallest path that exercises the full wire chain (handshake\-derived profile + DisplayService encoder + Device.send). Useful diagnostic for confirming a device class works end\-to\-end on real hardware.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBHEX_COLOR\fR
Hex color (e.g. ff0000 for red)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS configure\-slideshow
.PP
\fBtrcc display configure\-slideshow\fR \fIKEY\fR \fITHEMES\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Set the slideshow theme list + interval.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBTHEMES\fR
Theme names (directories under user_content_dir)  \-  order matters
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Seconds between theme swaps (default 60).
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS keepalive
.PP
\fBtrcc display keepalive\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Periodically resend the device's last frame. Workaround for Bulk/LY firmware that drops the displayed image when the internal buffer ages out. Render at least once before starting the loop so there's a cached frame to resend. count=0 (default) runs open\-ended and exits cleanly on Ctrl\-C  \-  the Command itself owns the loop + signal handling so the CLI doesn't need a user\-space while wrapper.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Seconds between resends. Bulk/LY firmware reverts to the built\-in logo after ~2\-3 s without a frame; default 0.150 s keeps the screen pinned.
.TP
\fB\-\-count, \-c \fICOUNT\fR\fR
Number of resends; 0 means loop forever (until Ctrl\-C).
.TP
\fB\-\-metric\-interval \fIMETRIC_INTERVAL\fR\fR
Seconds between overlay re\-renders (live sensor refresh). 0 disables  \-  last frame's metrics stay frozen on screen.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS list\-masks
.PP
\fBtrcc display list\-masks\fR [\fIKEY\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List mask images for the device's resolution. By default, scans both the cloud\-downloaded mask dir (data/web/zt{W}{H}) and the user\-created mask dir (user_content_dir/data/web/zt{W}{H}).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key (e.g. 0402:3922)  \-  its resolution scopes the scan. Required unless \-\-dir is given.
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-dir, \-d \fIDIRECTORY\fR\fR
Override: scan an explicit directory instead of the device's mask dirs
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS load\-image
.PP
\fBtrcc display load\-image\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR
.PP
Show a single image on the LCD. Stages the image as a one\-file theme so the existing render pipeline handles fit + brightness + rotation. Re\-runnable: subsequent loads of the same image are cheap (no re\-copy).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Image file (PNG / JPG / JPEG / BMP / WEBP)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS load\-theme
.PP
\fBtrcc display load\-theme\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR
.PP
Load a theme: parse, persist, render+send if device is connected.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Theme directory
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS load\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display load\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Play a video on the LCD as a single\-video theme. Transcodes the source to a Theme.zt matching the device's native resolution (.zt inputs are copied as\-is), stages a one\-file theme, then dispatches LoadTheme. Device must be attached so we know the target resolution.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Video file (MP4 / MOV / WEBM / MKV / AVI / ZT)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-start, \-s \fISTART_MS\fR\fR
Clip start in milliseconds (default: 0).
.TP
\fB\-\-end, \-e \fIEND_MS\fR\fR
Clip end in milliseconds (default: probe duration, fallback 10s).
.TP
\fB\-\-rotation, \-r \fIROTATION\fR\fR
Rotation in degrees: 0 / 90 / 180 / 270.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS loop\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display loop\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Toggle whether video wraps at the end or sticks at the last frame.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' (loop) or 'off' (single\-pass)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS mask\-position
.PP
\fBtrcc display mask\-position\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIX\fR \fIY\fR
.PP
Position the mask overlay within the canvas.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBX\fR
X offset in pixels (>= 0)
.TP
\fBY\fR
Y offset in pixels (>= 0)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS mask\-visible
.PP
\fBtrcc display mask\-visible\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Toggle mask visibility.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' or 'off'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Toggle the metric overlay layer.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' or 'off'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-add
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-add\fR \fIKEY\fR \fITYPE_\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Add a user\-edited overlay element to a device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBTYPE_\fR
\&'text' / 'metric' / 'clock'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-x \fIX\fR\fR
X position
.TP
\fB\-\-y \fIY\fR\fR
Y position
.TP
\fB\-\-text \fITEXT\fR\fR
Text content (type=text)
.TP
\fB\-\-metric \fIMETRIC\fR\fR
Metric id (type=metric)
.TP
\fB\-\-format \fIFMT\fR\fR
Metric format string
.TP
\fB\-\-source \fISOURCE\fR\fR
Clock source: time / weekday / date
.TP
\fB\-\-color \fICOLOR\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-size \fISIZE\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-bold\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-italic\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-unit\fR
Draw the metric's unit ( degC/%/MHz/RPM) after the number, or the bare number when the unit is baked into the theme art
.TP
\fB\-\-id \fIELEMENT_ID\fR\fR
Explicit element id (default: auto\-generated UUID)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-background
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-background\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIHEX_COLOR\fR
.PP
Set the solid color used when background\-mode=color.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBHEX_COLOR\fR
Hex color (e.g. 000000 for black)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-delete
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-delete\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIELEMENT_ID\fR
.PP
Remove a user\-edited overlay element by id.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fBELEMENT_ID\fR
ID returned by overlay\-add
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-flash
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-flash\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIELEMENT_ID\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Briefly highlight an overlay element in the GUI.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fBELEMENT_ID\fR
(no description)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-duration, \-d \fIDURATION_MS\fR\fR
Flash duration in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-render
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-render\fR \fIDC_PATH\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Render a DC config to a PNG preview  \-  no active device required. Mirrors legacy trcc overlay  \-  composites every element from config1.dc onto a solid\-black canvas at *width x height* and writes the result as PNG. Useful when iterating on a theme's metric positions without unplugging the device or sending frames.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBDC_PATH\fR
DC file or theme directory containing config1.dc
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-output, \-o \fIOUTPUT\fR\fR
Output PNG path for the rendered preview.
.TP
\fB\-\-width, \-w \fIWIDTH\fR\fR
Render canvas width (px)
.TP
\fB\-\-height, \-h \fIHEIGHT\fR\fR
Render canvas height (px)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS overlay\-update
.PP
\fBtrcc display overlay\-update\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIELEMENT_ID\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Mutate fields on an existing user\-edited overlay element.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fBELEMENT_ID\fR
ID returned by overlay\-add
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-x \fIX\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-y \fIY\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-color \fICOLOR\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-size \fISIZE\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-text \fITEXT\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-metric \fIMETRIC\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-format \fIFMT\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-source \fISOURCE\fR\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-bold\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-italic\fR
(no description)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-unit\fR
Draw the metric's unit ( degC/%/MHz/RPM) after the number, or the bare number when the unit is baked into the theme art
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS pause\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display pause\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Pause or resume video playback.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' (pause) or 'off' (resume)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS play
.PP
\fBtrcc display play\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Run the render\-and\-send ticker until Ctrl\-C. Dispatches RenderAndSend every tick with live sensors. Keeps SCSI devices from timing out (static\-blink fix) and advances video playback. Stops cleanly on SIGINT.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Tick interval in seconds (default: AppSettings.refresh_interval_s)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS play\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display play\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Decode a video and start playing it on the device. Overrides the active theme's background until stop\-video runs. Frames advance on each display play tick.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Video path (mp4/mov/webm/mkv/avi/zt)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-fps \fIFPS\fR\fR
Decode FPS (default: 15)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS restore\-theme
.PP
\fBtrcc display restore\-theme\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Reload the device's persisted theme  \-  convenience after restart.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS resume
.PP
\fBtrcc display resume\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Send each detected device's last\-used theme (headless, no GUI). Use case: cron / systemd unit / udev hook that runs at boot or after a suspend cycle. Enumerates every TRCC\-known device on the bus, connects, and replays the saved theme so the displays come back to their pre\-boot / pre\-suspend state without the GUI. Bulk/LY devices fade after ~2\-3 s without a fresh frame  \-  pair this with trcc display keepalive per device for those, or trcc display play for the full render\-loop.
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-retries \fIRETRIES\fR\fR
Discovery attempts before giving up (1 attempt = 2 s delay)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS screencast
.PP
\fBtrcc display screencast\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIX\fR \fIY\fR \fIW\fR \fIH\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Stream a screen region to the LCD until interrupted. Wraps StartScreencast  \-  the GUI ScreencastHandler subscriber drives the per\-frame Qt capture timer. Ctrl\-C calls StopScreencast for clean teardown.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBX\fR
Top\-left X coordinate of capture region (px)
.TP
\fBY\fR
Top\-left Y coordinate of capture region (px)
.TP
\fBW\fR
Capture region width (px)
.TP
\fBH\fR
Capture region height (px)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-audio\fR
Pipe system audio alongside the video feed (Linux: PipeWire)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS seek\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display seek\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIFRAME\fR
.PP
Jump the playback cursor to a specific frame.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key
.TP
\fBFRAME\fR
Frame index to jump to
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS send\-image
.PP
\fBtrcc display send\-image\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPATH\fR
.PP
Push an image to the LCD once  \-  no theme staging, no persistence. Companion to load\-image (which materialises a single\-image theme and persists DeviceSettings.current_theme). Use this when you want ephemeral display: boot logos, quick previews, API upload pipelines.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Image file (PNG/JPG/BMP/WEBP)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS set\-brightness
.PP
\fBtrcc display set\-brightness\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIPERCENT\fR
.PP
Set per\-device display brightness.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBPERCENT\fR
Brightness 0\-100
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS set\-fit\-mode
.PP
\fBtrcc display set\-fit\-mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIMODE\fR
.PP
Set how the background fits the canvas.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBMODE\fR
Fit mode: 'width' (letterbox), 'height' (pillarbox), 'stretch'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS set\-orientation
.PP
\fBtrcc display set\-orientation\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIDEGREES\fR
.PP
Set per\-device rotation.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBDEGREES\fR
Rotation: 0, 90, 180, or 270
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS sleep
.PP
\fBtrcc display sleep\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Blank the panel so it goes dark (the shutdown / turn\-off action). Sends a solid\-black frame (LCD) or an all\-off payload (LED)  \-  the same Command the GUI + daemon fire at PC shutdown so the screen doesn't hold its last image lit. Idempotent; auto\-connects in a fresh process.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS slideshow
.PP
\fBtrcc display slideshow\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISTATE\fR
.PP
Toggle the per\-device slideshow on/off.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBSTATE\fR
\&'on' / 'off'
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS slideshow\-run
.PP
\fBtrcc display slideshow\-run\fR \fIKEY\fR \fITHEMES_DIR\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Foreground slideshow over a directory of themes. Different from slideshow / configure\-slideshow (which persist state). This is a one\-shot loop: blocks until Ctrl\-C, swaps to the next theme each tick. Useful for demos + smoke tests; the persisted flow is what production users want.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBTHEMES_DIR\fR
Directory containing theme subdirectories
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-interval, \-i \fIINTERVAL\fR\fR
Seconds between theme switches (default: 30.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS snapshot
.PP
\fBtrcc display snapshot\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Print the persisted LCD state for a device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON instead of human text.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS split\-mode
.PP
\fBtrcc display split\-mode\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIMODE\fR
.PP
Set the Dynamic Island style (widescreen panels only).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.TP
\fBMODE\fR
0 (off), 1 (style A), 2 (B), 3 (C)
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS stop\-screencast
.PP
\fBtrcc display stop\-screencast\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Stop an active screencast started by another process (daemon/API).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS stop\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display stop\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Clear the video playback override (returns to the active theme).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS test
.PP
\fBtrcc display test\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Color\-cycle the LCD: red \-> green \-> blue \-> black. Smallest end\-to\-end exercise of the wire chain. Useful when porting a new device class to confirm handshake \-> frame build \-> USB send all work before fighting overlay/theme bugs.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-seconds, \-s \fISECONDS\fR\fR
Hold each color for this many seconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS test\-lcd
.PP
\fBtrcc display test\-lcd\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Print an ANSI true\-color preview of the LCD's current render. Same pipeline as display play but stops at the renderer surface  \-  no wire send. Useful for headless / sshell debugging where you can't see the physical device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key, e.g. 0402:3922
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-cols, \-c \fICOLS\fR\fR
Width of the ANSI preview in terminal cells.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS toggle\-video
.PP
\fBtrcc display toggle\-video\fR \fIKEY\fR
.PP
Flip video playback between paused / playing (single\-verb helper).
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
.SS upload\-mask
.PP
\fBtrcc display upload\-mask\fR \fIKEY\fR \fISOURCE\fR
.PP
Copy a mask into user_content_dir/masks and apply it to the device.
.PP
Arguments:
.RS 4
.TP
\fBKEY\fR
Device key
.TP
\fBSOURCE\fR
Mask image file to copy + apply
.RE
.PP
Options:
.RS 4
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this command's help and exit.
.RE
